   "notes": "Standard third-order Birch-Murnaghan pressure-volume EOS in the Eulerian finite-strain convention at 300 K. V0=179.2(7) A^3 and K0=207(5) GPa were constrained using the source's K*V systematics; K0_prime=4.4 was fixed. Parenthesized EOS errors are stored as generic published uncertainties because the article gives no confidence level or covariance matrix. The alternative K0_prime=4 sensitivity fit (V0=175.9(6) A^3, K0=245(5) GPa) and the separate 0 K DFT BM3 are documented by the source but are not bundled as additional records here. The experimental envelope is not a phase-stability guarantee, and the high-pressure structure is metastably retained during room-temperature decompression."
  }
